---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s23b-layer-storage-commands"
  chapter="Layers"
  title="Storage — Commands"
  notes="Volume triage: pvc/pv, describe pvc, describe pod mount events, storageclass, volumeattachments. Myth: PVC Bound means volume works — binding ≠ mounted."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <section>
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-cyan">Typical commands</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        caption="Volume triage"
        code={`kubectl get pvc,pv -n <ns>
kubectl describe pvc <claim> -n <ns>
kubectl describe pod <pod> -n <ns>   # Mount events
kubectl get storageclass
kubectl get volumeattachments   # CSI attach state`}
      />
    </section>

    <Callout type="myth">
      PVC Bound means the volume works. Binding ≠ mounted. Mount failures and permission errors appear only in pod events.
    </Callout>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-deck-border/60 pt-4">
      <Pill tone="amber">Decision hint</Pill>
      <span class="text-lg text-deck-muted">ContainerCreating + volume → describe pod events, not just PVC status.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Slide>
